        ['The 3rd term of an AP is 11 and the 7th term is 23. Find (a) the first term and common difference, (b) the 20th term, (c) the sum of the first 20 terms.', ['Equations', 'a and d', '20th term', 'Sum'], '(a) a + 2d = 11, a + 6d = 23, so 4d = 12, d = 3, a = 5. (b) T₂₀ = 5 + 19(3) = 62. (c) S₂₀ = 20/2 (5 + 62) = 670.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 10],
        ['The first term of a GP is 3 and the common ratio is 2. Find (a) the 8th term, (b) the sum of the first 8 terms, (c) the least number of terms whose sum exceeds 1,000.', ['T8', 'S8', 'Inequality', 'n = 9'], '(a) T₈ = 3 × 2⁷ = 384. (b) S₈ = 3(2⁸ − 1)/1 = 765. (c) 3(2ⁿ − 1) > 1000, 2ⁿ > 334.3, n = 9.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['Find the sum to infinity of the series 12 + 6 + 3 + 1.5 + … and the value of n for which the nth term is 3/16.', ['r', 'S∞', 'Equation', 'n'], 'a = 12, r = 1/2, S∞ = 12/(1 − 1/2) = 24. 12(1/2)ⁿ⁻¹ = 3/16, (1/2)ⁿ⁻¹ = 1/64, so n − 1 = 6 and n = 7.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['Show that the sum of the first n odd numbers is n².', ['AP', 'Formula', 'Simplify'], 'The odd numbers form an AP with a = 1 and d = 2. Sₙ = n/2 [2 + 2(n − 1)] = n/2 × 2n = n².', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 6],
