        ['How many four-digit numbers can be formed from the digits 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 if no digit is repeated? How many of them are even?', ['Total 360', 'Even 180'], 'Total = 6P4 = 360. Even numbers: the last digit is 2, 4 or 6 (3 choices), the remaining three places are filled in 5P3 = 60 ways, so 3 × 60 = 180.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A committee of 5 is to be chosen from 6 men and 4 women. Find the number of committees containing (a) exactly 2 women, (b) at least 3 women.', ['Exactly 2', '3 women', '4 women', 'Total'], '(a) 4C2 × 6C3 = 6 × 20 = 120. (b) 3 women: 4C3 × 6C2 = 60; 4 women: 4C4 × 6C1 = 6; total 66.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['In how many ways can the letters of the word MATHEMATICS be arranged?', ['n!', 'Repeats', 'Answer'], 'There are 11 letters with M, A and T each appearing twice, so 11!/(2! 2! 2!) = 4,989,600.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 6],
        ['Show that ⁿCᵣ + ⁿCᵣ₊₁ = ⁿ⁺¹Cᵣ₊₁.', ['Common denominator', 'Simplify'], 'LHS = n!/[r!(n − r)!] + n!/[(r + 1)!(n − r − 1)!] = n!/[(r + 1)!(n − r)!] × [(r + 1) + (n − r)] = (n + 1)!/[(r + 1)!(n − r)!] = ⁿ⁺¹Cᵣ₊₁.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 6],
        ['Five boys and three girls are to sit in a row. Find the number of arrangements in which the three girls sit together.', ['Block', 'Arrange', 'Total'], 'Treat the girls as one block: 6 objects can be arranged in 6! = 720 ways and the girls among themselves in 3! = 6 ways, so 720 × 6 = 4,320.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 6],
