        ['Show that (x − 2) is a factor of f(x) = x³ − 3x² − 4x + 12 and factorise f(x) completely.', ['f(2)', 'Division', 'Factorise'], 'f(2) = 8 − 12 − 8 + 12 = 0, so (x − 2) is a factor. Dividing gives x² − x − 6 = (x − 3)(x + 2). Hence f(x) = (x − 2)(x − 3)(x + 2).', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['When x³ + px² + qx + 6 is divided by (x − 1) the remainder is 12, and (x + 2) is a factor. Find p and q.', ['Two equations', 'Solve', 'p and q'], 'f(1) = 1 + p + q + 6 = 12, so p + q = 5. f(−2) = −8 + 4p − 2q + 6 = 0, so 2p − q = 1. Adding: 3p = 6, p = 2 and q = 3.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
