        ['Divide x³ + 2x² − 5x − 6 by (x + 1) and state the quotient and remainder.', ['Division', 'Remainder'], 'Long division gives quotient x² + x − 6 and remainder 0, so x³ + 2x² − 5x − 6 = (x + 1)(x + 3)(x − 2).', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 6],
        ['State the remainder and factor theorems and show how the factor theorem follows from the remainder theorem.', ['Remainder', 'Factor', 'Link'], 'Remainder theorem: when f(x) is divided by (x − a), the remainder is f(a). Factor theorem: (x − a) is a factor if and only if f(a) = 0. If the remainder f(a) is zero the division is exact, so (x − a) divides f(x).', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 6],
