        ['Express (5x + 1)/[(x − 1)(x + 2)] in partial fractions.', ['Form', 'A', 'B', 'Result'], 'Let (5x + 1)/[(x − 1)(x + 2)] = A/(x − 1) + B/(x + 2). Then 5x + 1 = A(x + 2) + B(x − 1). Put x = 1: 6 = 3A, A = 2. Put x = −2: −9 = −3B, B = 3. Hence 2/(x − 1) + 3/(x + 2).', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['Express (3x² + 2)/[x(x + 1)(x − 2)] in partial fractions.', ['A', 'B', 'C', 'Result'], 'Write A/x + B/(x + 1) + C/(x − 2). Put x = 0: A = 2/(−2) = −1. Put x = −1: B = 5/[(−1)(−3)] = 5/3. Put x = 2: C = 14/(2 × 3) = 7/3. So −1/x + (5/3)/(x + 1) + (7/3)/(x − 2).', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['Express (x² + 1)/[(x − 1)(x + 1)] in the form A + B/(x − 1) + C/(x + 1).', ['Divide', 'Partial fractions', 'Result'], 'The fraction is improper: (x² + 1)/(x² − 1) = 1 + 2/(x² − 1) = 1 + 1/(x − 1) − 1/(x + 1).', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 8],
        ['Express (2x + 3)/(x + 1)² in partial fractions.', ['Form', 'A', 'B'], '(2x + 3)/(x + 1)² = A/(x + 1) + B/(x + 1)². 2x + 3 = A(x + 1) + B gives A = 2 and 2 + B = 3, so B = 1. Hence 2/(x + 1) + 1/(x + 1)².', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 6],
        ['Use partial fractions to evaluate the sum 1/(1·2) + 1/(2·3) + … + 1/(n(n + 1)).', ['Decompose', 'Telescope', 'Result'], '1/(r(r + 1)) = 1/r − 1/(r + 1); the sum telescopes to 1 − 1/(n + 1) = n/(n + 1).', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 6],
